{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model first development model first development","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","fileName":"Model-First Development.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model-First Development","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Modeling]] [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Database-First Development","Code-First Development","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model first development model first development","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","fileName":"Model-First Development.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model-First Development","heading":"Model-First Development","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Model-first development begins with a visual or conceptual data model and generates a database schema from it. The model is the primary design artifact, so database changes follow changes made through the modeling tools.\n\nThe approach can make relationships visually approachable, but it depends on suitable tooling and generated artifacts. It differs from [[Database-First Development]], which begins with an existing database, and [[Code-First Development]], which begins with entity classes.\n\nThe EF Core 3 discussion places model-first in historical contrast with the framework's code-centered workflow. A separately maintained visual model is not treated as the authoritative round-trip design surface in the project.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Database-First Development","Code-First Development","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model first development model first development","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model-First Development.md","fileName":"Model-First Development.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model-First Development","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Modeling","Entity Framework Core Data Access","Database-First Development","Code-First Development","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}